From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qwqgong-ui <noreply@qwqgong-ui.local>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 14:40:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] system: let the handler report an ICMP error for a UDP
 flow

A datagram the handler cannot forward produces no signal of its own. The
sender is talking to a tun device that accepted the packet, so nothing
tells it the path could not carry it: it keeps sending the same size, or
waits out a timeout that a Destination Unreachable would have ended
immediately. Path MTU discovery is the case that matters - IPv6 has no
in-network fragmentation, so a path smaller than what the sender picked
is a blackhole until the sender's own probing gives up.

The stack is exactly where a router that could not forward the datagram
stands, and it is the only place that still holds the IP and UDP headers
such an error has to quote, so give the handler a way to ask for one:
ReportICMPError on the packet writer it already holds, with the four
conditions worth reporting. The error is sent from the address the
sender's own route points at - the stack's own next address, the first
hop as far as the sender is concerned - falling back to the address the
sender was trying to reach when the stack has none on that family.

Only the system stack implements it; gvisor builds its write back through
a stack route rather than by hand.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 stack_system.go        |   4 +
 udp_icmp_error.go      | 180 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 udp_icmp_error_test.go | 149 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 333 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 udp_icmp_error.go
 create mode 100644 udp_icmp_error_test.go

